      "message": "Note that this is *not* the same as NetworkInfo#isConnected. That method will return false for a network that is currently suspended, but nai.everConnected will return true.\n\nWhether this is fixing a bug, adding a bug, or neither depends on what the caller wants to do with the result. I\u0027m not sure we have enough information here to decide. But if we audit all the callers of getAllNetworkState (I think there are only 2 or 3) then this might be correct. Did you do that? If so, you should probably mention that in the commit message instead of saying \"So the callers don\u0027t need to reference to NetworkInfo.isConnected() anymore.\"",
